{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note_main",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": 0, "y": -175 },
      "style": { "width": 1600, "height": 160 },
      "width": 1600, "height": 160,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 1,
          "text": "**MC Water Mask Validation vs River Shapefiles**  ·  from `MC_mask_validation_NEW.py`\n\nValidates MC P(water) against two reference shapefiles: river extent *with* bridges (wider polygon) and *without* bridges (clean water only).\nBridge pixels = with_bridges ∩ ¬no_bridges. Open water = no_bridges polygon.\n\n**Setup**\n1. `water_prob_mc.tif` → **MC Probability** reader (defines the pixel grid).\n2. Pre-computed index TIFs (mndwi_base.tif etc.) → respective readers.\n3. Set shapefile paths in **with_bridges** and **no_bridges** rasterizers.\n4. `sci_mask_metrics` nodes compare MC mask vs each reference at P≥0.7.\n5. `py_cdf` renders CDF + threshold-sweep figure. `py_idx_compute` builds metrics DataFrames → **ml_bar_chart** nodes render F1/IoU bars per reference."
        }
      }
    },

    {
      "id": "frame_inputs",
      "type": "canvas_frame",
      "position": { "x": -20, "y": -20 },
      "style": { "width": 320, "height": 1440, "zIndex": -1 },
      "width": 320, "height": 1440,
      "data": { "label": "Frame", "params": { "title": "Input rasters & shapefiles", "color_index": 0 } }
    },
